1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:02,310
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:03,740
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,810 --> 00:00:05,240
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,780
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

5
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:08,850
Next, please.

6
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:12,820
- Name, please?
- It's Ko Eun Seol.

7
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:16,320
Is this based on your first draft?

8
00:00:17,190 --> 00:00:18,190
Of course.

9
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:51,460
You're all set.
Your registration number is 97.

10
00:00:52,090 --> 00:00:54,490
- Okay, thank you.
- Thank you.

11
00:00:58,630 --> 00:00:59,730
(Application Desk)

12
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:00,800
Next.

13
00:01:01,870 --> 00:01:06,240
(Cheongma Group's Open Competition
for New Designers)

14
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:12,340
Wait. Where is he?

15
00:01:19,650 --> 00:01:20,650
Seok Jin, where are you?

16
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:22,290
Meet me in the parking garage.

17
00:01:23,050 --> 00:01:24,060
Okay.

18
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:35,130
I thought the airport was it,
but here we are again.

19
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:39,600
Have you been well?

20
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:42,910
As you can tell.

21
00:01:46,950 --> 00:01:47,950
You?

22
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:52,320
I've been well too.

23
00:01:54,050 --> 00:01:55,490
In what way?

24
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,060
Never mind.

25
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,600
I guess I don't need to know that.

26
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:09,900
I'm sorry.

27
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:11,940
Don't be.

28
00:02:12,570 --> 00:02:14,070
It's all in the past anyway.

29
00:02:19,940 --> 00:02:22,480
It looked like
you were entering the competition.

30
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:24,750
Yes.

31
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:27,220
I hope it goes well for you.

32
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,560
See you.

33
00:02:57,980 --> 00:02:59,120
What's her deal?

34
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:18,870
In what way?

35
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:25,180
Never mind.

36
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:27,780
I guess I don't need to know that.

37
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:33,020
I'm sorry.

38
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:35,020
Don't be.

39
00:03:35,690 --> 00:03:37,090
It's all in the past anyway.

40
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:06,020
Feels like it's been ages
since we drank alone together.

41
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:08,320
This is great, isn't it?

42
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:11,460
Seok Jin.

43
00:04:11,490 --> 00:04:12,490
Yes?

44
00:04:13,290 --> 00:04:14,290
What's with that look on your face?

45
00:04:14,830 --> 00:04:15,930
What about it?

46
00:04:18,030 --> 00:04:19,830
Did something happen
while you were waiting for me?

47
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:21,400
No.

48
00:04:21,830 --> 00:04:23,170
You look kind of angry.

49
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:26,970
What's there to be angry about?
I'm just a little tired.

50
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:30,270
That's why I told you
to take it easy at work.

51
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:39,220
How are
the competition entries looking?

52
00:04:41,190 --> 00:04:42,820
It's a blind review,
so I haven't seen the profiles,

53
00:04:42,890 --> 00:04:44,260
but the quality of the work
seems high.

54
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:47,590
The only thing that matters
is picking the right winner,

55
00:04:48,290 --> 00:04:49,790
since they'll be working
directly under me.

56
00:05:00,470 --> 00:05:01,540
Hey, Dad.

57
00:05:02,470 --> 00:05:04,010
I'm at a friend's birthday party.

58
00:05:04,710 --> 00:05:07,050
Are you calling
because you're worried about me?

59
00:05:08,250 --> 00:05:09,750
Okay. I'll be home soon.

60
00:05:10,450 --> 00:05:11,450
Sure.

61
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:16,990
Why did you lie?

62
00:05:17,820 --> 00:05:20,690
I'm being smart
to buy you some time.

63
00:05:28,430 --> 00:05:29,430
Who is it?

64
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:32,540
CEO Kang.

65
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:35,440
Seriously? Tell him you're at home.

66
00:05:40,710 --> 00:05:41,780
Just answer it already.

67
00:05:42,350 --> 00:05:43,350
I don't want to lie.

68
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:45,180
Seok Jin.

69
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:46,720
Let's go.

70
00:05:47,150 --> 00:05:48,150
Seok Jin.

71
00:05:54,190 --> 00:05:56,560
The person you are trying to reach
is unavailable.

72
00:05:56,730 --> 00:05:58,500
What is it? Isn't he answering?

73
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:01,300
He's likely not answering
so he doesn't have to lie.

74
00:06:02,130 --> 00:06:03,970
This is another thing
I hate about him.

75
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:08,010
What's that supposed to mean?

76
00:06:08,210 --> 00:06:10,910
If he cares about Hae Ra,
he should be willing to lie for her.

77
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:12,480
But he can't even do that.

78
00:06:12,910 --> 00:06:15,010
Why are you blowing this
out of proportion?

79
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:16,950
He probably just can't
get to the phone right now.

80
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:20,350
Besides, Hae Ra said
she's at a birthday party.

81
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:24,590
- And you believe that?
- What else am I to do?

82
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:27,630
And just opposing them
isn't the answer.

83
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:30,700
Hae Ra thinks she's Juliet, I swear.

84
00:06:31,130 --> 00:06:34,300
The tragic heroine who died because
her parents opposed her marriage.

85
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:38,570
That's not to say
she's actually going to die.

86
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:41,540
It just means
we have to tread lightly with her.

87
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:43,140
Just forget it.

88
00:06:43,510 --> 00:06:47,150
Why don't you try harder
to find a match for Hae Ra?

89
00:06:47,410 --> 00:06:48,950
What good are
all your connections...

90
00:06:49,010 --> 00:06:50,250
if you don't use them
for things like this?

91
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:52,280
Find someone.

92
00:06:57,290 --> 00:06:58,660
Mi Ran, what do you think?

93
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:01,190
Do you really think
Seok Jin didn't answer...

94
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:02,730
because he didn't want to lie?

95
00:07:03,530 --> 00:07:04,660
I'm not sure.

96
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:08,000
But if he had answered and lied,

97
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:10,740
the CEO would've been mad at him
for lying anyway.

98
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:12,970
I guess that's true.

99
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:15,910
If you look for faults,
you'll always find them.

100
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:27,750
What's her deal?

101
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:34,630
By the way,
is something bothering you?

102
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:36,830
You've got a look on your face.

103
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:40,260
Who, me? Bothered?

104
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:41,700
Not at all.

105
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:50,270
Were you with Seok Jin?

106
00:07:50,780 --> 00:07:51,810
How did you know?

107
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:55,980
He can't even tell
one little lie for you?

108
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:58,480
That just made me
fall for him harder.

109
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:02,190
Don't you just love a man
who can't lie?

110
00:08:03,290 --> 00:08:06,890
When you're blinded by love,
everything seems wonderful.

111
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:10,560
I saw Ko Eun Seol on my way out.

112
00:08:11,330 --> 00:08:13,230
Who was it that you saw?
Ko Eun Seol?

113
00:08:14,070 --> 00:08:15,070
Yes.

114
00:08:17,030 --> 00:08:18,570
She said she wants to work
for our company.

115
00:08:18,970 --> 00:08:20,270
Does she think
if she hangs around the office,

116
00:08:20,340 --> 00:08:22,410
someone will just hand her a job?

117
00:08:23,310 --> 00:08:26,540
I think she's entering
the open design competition.

118
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:27,950
What?

119
00:08:29,110 --> 00:08:31,220
The second round of submissions
is due today.

120
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:33,720
Wasn't she pretty good at painting?

121
00:08:37,790 --> 00:08:38,790
Well, look who it is.

122
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:49,930
It really is you, Ko Eun Seol.

123
00:08:51,270 --> 00:08:52,440
Oh, right.

124
00:08:53,570 --> 00:08:54,770
This is your family's company,
isn't it?

125
00:08:56,310 --> 00:08:57,340
It's been a while.

126
00:08:57,940 --> 00:08:59,080
How have you been?

127
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:00,580
Are you married?

128
00:09:00,950 --> 00:09:01,950
No, not yet.

129
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,080
Then what about work?

130
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:05,920
I'm looking for a job.

131
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:08,450
I see. You're unemployed.

132
00:09:11,390 --> 00:09:12,560
So what brings you here?

133
00:09:12,890 --> 00:09:14,630
I told you. I'm looking for a job.

134
00:09:15,030 --> 00:09:16,330
I want to work here.

135
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:19,160
You're right. That has to be it.

136
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:22,200
Since the winner gets hired,
that's what she's after.

137
00:09:23,670 --> 00:09:24,940
What are you going to do now?

138
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:26,740
What else?

139
00:09:27,610 --> 00:09:28,670
I have to stop her.

140
00:09:47,830 --> 00:09:49,290
Mom!

141
00:09:51,630 --> 00:09:53,530
Somebody help me.

142
00:09:54,030 --> 00:09:56,230
Please, Mom...

143
00:09:56,300 --> 00:10:01,040
Oh no, what do I do? Mom!

144
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,790
I have to find out the truth.

145
00:10:21,190 --> 00:10:22,690
I'll never stop until I do.

146
00:10:38,780 --> 00:10:40,680
Do you have the list of portfolios
that were submitted yesterday?

147
00:10:40,850 --> 00:10:41,980
Bring it to me.

148
00:10:42,410 --> 00:10:44,080
What for, Ms. Kang?

149
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:46,880
Stop asking questions
and just do what you're told.

150
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,130
Here it is, Ms. Kang.

151
00:11:02,530 --> 00:11:04,640
(97. Ko Eun Seol)

152
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:06,470
Unbelievable.

153
00:11:07,810 --> 00:11:09,940
Have the portfolios been converted
to PDF files?

154
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:11,180
They're all done.

155
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,910
We were about to send them
to the judges.

156
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:16,850
For now, just send them my way.
I'll pass them along to the judges.

157
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:19,280
Sure.

158
00:11:41,570 --> 00:11:45,080
- Who is it?
- Oh, hello. I'm the realtor.

159
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:48,280
- The thing is...
- Hello there.

160
00:11:48,450 --> 00:11:50,920
This is the homeowner.

161
00:11:51,580 --> 00:11:52,650
- Hello.
- Hello.

162
00:11:52,650 --> 00:11:55,490
Anyway, I'm very sorry, but...

163
00:11:55,490 --> 00:11:56,490
Is this it?

164
00:11:58,060 --> 00:11:59,820
Yes, that's the annex.

165
00:12:00,830 --> 00:12:01,830
Let's take a look inside, Dad.

166
00:12:02,190 --> 00:12:03,660
Right, sure.

167
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:07,260
Excuse me. Hey, hold on.

168
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:11,640
Of all the places we've seen,
this one seems the best.

169
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:12,700
What do you think?

170
00:12:12,770 --> 00:12:14,540
- I guess it's not bad.
- Right.

171
00:12:14,710 --> 00:12:17,010
Grandma can have the master bedroom,

172
00:12:17,510 --> 00:12:19,540
and we can use
the room across the hall.

173
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:22,380
If you're satisfied,
shall we go sign the contract?

174
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:24,180
- Let's do that.
- Wait.

175
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:25,620
I'm sorry,

176
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:27,920
but this place
has already been taken.

177
00:12:28,190 --> 00:12:29,390
What do you mean it's taken?

178
00:12:29,690 --> 00:12:32,320
Wait, did you go
with another realtor?

179
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:34,090
No, that's not it.

180
00:12:34,730 --> 00:12:36,830
An acquaintance of mine
is moving in.

181
00:12:37,730 --> 00:12:39,400
An acquaintance of yours?

182
00:12:40,030 --> 00:12:41,170
Yes, I'm sorry.

183
00:12:42,170 --> 00:12:45,170
- I'm sorry.
- Is it because you don't like us?

184
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,000
What?

185
00:12:47,570 --> 00:12:49,210
What are you talking about?

186
00:12:49,670 --> 00:12:54,210
Are you only saying it's taken
because you don't approve of us?

187
00:12:55,550 --> 00:12:58,750
Talk about a chip on his shoulder.
That's not it at all.

188
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:01,290
Then show me the contract.

189
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:03,320
- Hey...
- Look here.

190
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:06,990
Didn't you hear me say
a friend was moving in?

191
00:13:06,990 --> 00:13:08,960
There's no contract.

192
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:12,630
Then I was right.
You're just making an excuse.

193
00:13:14,370 --> 00:13:15,900
That's no way to treat people.

194
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:18,070
You can't just blatantly
look down on us...

195
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:19,340
because we don't have much.

196
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:22,840
How am I looking down on you?
I'm not that kind of person.

197
00:13:23,210 --> 00:13:24,610
You're unbelievable.

198
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:27,480
- You're one to talk.
- Look here.

199
00:13:27,550 --> 00:13:29,810
- And see what?
- Hey, stop that.

200
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:31,750
What's gotten into you?

201
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:34,350
I'm so sorry about that.

202
00:13:34,820 --> 00:13:37,320
It's just that
our house was auctioned off,

203
00:13:37,390 --> 00:13:38,960
and we're in
a very difficult situation.

204
00:13:39,020 --> 00:13:41,290
Couldn't you please make
an exception for us?

205
00:13:42,490 --> 00:13:44,060
I wish I could.

206
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:46,530
But someone really is supposed
to move in.

207
00:13:48,330 --> 00:13:49,370
Forget it, Dad. Let's go.

208
00:13:49,630 --> 00:13:51,170
It's not like
this is the only house out there.

209
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:53,600
That's no way to live your life.

210
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:57,810
Are you kidding me?

211
00:14:01,650 --> 00:14:03,480
Excuse me. Hey!

212
00:14:03,950 --> 00:14:05,750
I told you that's not it.

213
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:06,820
What?

214
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:07,820
Attorney Seo?

215
00:14:07,990 --> 00:14:09,620
Eun Guk, hey.

216
00:14:10,090 --> 00:14:12,190
- Mr. Ko, hello.
- Gosh, hi.

217
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:14,560
Do you know them?

218
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:16,160
Oh.

219
00:14:16,260 --> 00:14:18,700
Sis, that's Eun Seol's
older brother and father.

220
00:14:19,230 --> 00:14:20,800
- What?
- Wait.

221
00:14:21,030 --> 00:14:23,000
Is this old lady your sister,
Attorney Seo?

222
00:14:24,130 --> 00:14:26,140
Hey, watch your mouth!

223
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:28,310
It's disrespectful to call her that.

224
00:14:28,910 --> 00:14:30,870
I'm sorry, pretty lady.

225
00:14:30,910 --> 00:14:33,440
- What...
- Mom, Uncle!

226
00:14:35,750 --> 00:14:37,510
I got my red belt today.

227
00:14:37,950 --> 00:14:39,780
Really? Good job.

228
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:40,780
Nice one.

229
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:44,150
- She's a mom, which makes her old.
- Right, she is.

230
00:14:46,390 --> 00:14:48,930
Let's not talk out here.
Please, come inside.

231
00:14:50,330 --> 00:14:51,360
What?

232
00:14:51,830 --> 00:14:54,330
Come on. Let's go inside.

233
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:56,400
Shall we?

234
00:14:57,070 --> 00:15:01,910
What? You're going to rent out
the annex to Eun Seol?

235
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:03,740
Yes.

236
00:15:05,210 --> 00:15:06,910
Then you should've just said so.

237
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:10,180
I believe I told you
a friend was moving in.

238
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:12,380
Well, I didn't know
you meant my sister.

239
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:13,880
Unbelievable.

240
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:16,350
I'm sorry for the misunderstanding.

241
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:18,160
What kind of person
do you take me for?

242
00:15:19,260 --> 00:15:20,290
In that case,

243
00:15:21,330 --> 00:15:22,330
could we also...

244
00:15:22,690 --> 00:15:23,930
move in?

245
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:26,100
Dad.

246
00:15:26,260 --> 00:15:29,000
It'd be a great chance
to live with Eun Seol again.

247
00:15:29,070 --> 00:15:30,500
She wouldn't be so lonely.

248
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:34,410
That's actually a great idea, sir.

249
00:15:34,410 --> 00:15:35,570
Hyun Jae...

250
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:37,880
If that's what you want to do,
go ahead.

251
00:15:38,310 --> 00:15:39,440
I'm fine either way.

252
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:40,640
Excuse me.

253
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:43,910
Who I rent out the annex to
is up to me.

254
00:15:43,980 --> 00:15:45,150
Don't get on your high horse...

255
00:15:45,150 --> 00:15:46,450
- just because you own a house.
- Hey!

256
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:48,720
Shut it. You're not helping.

257
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:52,590
Please, is there any way
you'd consider it?

258
00:15:53,990 --> 00:15:55,690
You were going
to let Eun Seol move in,

259
00:15:55,690 --> 00:15:56,830
so what's there to consider?

260
00:15:57,560 --> 00:15:58,760
Sounds good, sir.

261
00:15:59,330 --> 00:16:01,830
Oh, goodness.
Thank you, Attorney Seo.

262
00:16:01,830 --> 00:16:04,170
My gosh. Thank you so much, ma'am.

263
00:16:04,170 --> 00:16:07,540
I mean, young lady...
What should I call you?

264
00:16:09,310 --> 00:16:10,540
- Thank you so much.
- Please, have some.

265
00:16:10,610 --> 00:16:11,610
Right.

266
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:15,310
You want me to live with you too?

267
00:16:15,780 --> 00:16:17,410
Why? Don't you want to?

268
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:23,150
Is it because you'd be living
with your grandmother?

269
00:16:24,890 --> 00:16:26,320
I don't know.

270
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:29,730
Your grandmother is much weaker now.

271
00:16:29,990 --> 00:16:32,130
She won't be like she used to be.
Besides,

272
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:35,130
you have me and Eun Guk,
so what's there to worry about?

273
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:41,840
You really don't want to?

274
00:16:43,410 --> 00:16:44,410
That's not it.

275
00:16:44,710 --> 00:16:47,610
Of course, I'd feel safe and happy
living with you and Eun Guk.

276
00:16:48,150 --> 00:16:50,050
Okay. Let's do it.

277
00:16:50,350 --> 00:16:51,920
Great. You made the right choice.

278
00:16:52,450 --> 00:16:53,750
We'll take care of the moving,

279
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:55,820
so just bring your own things.
All right?

280
00:16:56,190 --> 00:16:57,190
Okay.

281
00:16:57,820 --> 00:17:00,090
- I'm sure you're busy, so go on.
- Sure.

282
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:06,630
What is it? You again?

283
00:17:07,330 --> 00:17:08,600
I'll get going then.

284
00:17:09,130 --> 00:17:11,340
All right. Get home safe.

285
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:15,870
Why not just have her
move in with us?

286
00:17:17,010 --> 00:17:19,310
- Actually, that's the plan, Mom.
- What?

287
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:23,710
We're all going to live together
at our new place.

288
00:17:25,180 --> 00:17:26,820
No, I refuse.

289
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:29,550
I'm terrified of living with her.

290
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:30,720
Mom!

291
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:33,020
Stop saying whatever comes to mind.

292
00:17:33,390 --> 00:17:34,830
How on earth could you say that?

293
00:17:34,830 --> 00:17:35,830
Whatever.

294
00:17:35,930 --> 00:17:38,260
I can't live with Eun Seol,
and that's final.

295
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:48,570
(Cheongma)

296
00:17:48,770 --> 00:17:51,540
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

297
00:17:52,710 --> 00:17:56,080
(Design Competition:
2nd Round Portfolio)

298
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:02,420
(Attached Files)

299
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:10,090
Where's 97?

300
00:18:14,030 --> 00:18:15,670
Yes, Design Team speaking.

301
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:18,200
Yes, hello.

302
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:19,800
Right.

303
00:18:20,770 --> 00:18:21,770
Pardon?

304
00:18:21,940 --> 00:18:23,710
File number 97 is missing?

305
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:25,110
One moment, please.

306
00:18:25,780 --> 00:18:28,910
Excuse me, Ms. Kang.
It's Judge Kim Hong Joo.

307
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:31,010
Apparently,
file number 97 is missing.

308
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:34,820
Say we didn't send it because
it violated judging guidelines.

309
00:18:35,250 --> 00:18:36,250
Sure.

310
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:38,320
Because it violated
the judging guidelines,

311
00:18:38,390 --> 00:18:40,260
our team leader had it pulled.

312
00:18:41,290 --> 00:18:42,290
Thank you.

313
00:18:43,890 --> 00:18:45,900
How did it violate
the judging guidelines?

314
00:18:57,740 --> 00:18:58,840
Hey, Seok Jin.

315
00:18:58,940 --> 00:19:00,840
File number 97 is missing.

316
00:19:03,110 --> 00:19:05,120
I disqualified it
for violating the guidelines.

317
00:19:05,750 --> 00:19:06,820
What guideline did it violate?

318
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:09,250
It didn't follow
the established rules.

319
00:19:09,950 --> 00:19:12,320
Is that so? All right.

320
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:22,070
You're all set.
Your registration number is 97.

321
00:19:22,470 --> 00:19:24,970
- Okay, thank you.
- Thank you.

322
00:19:29,910 --> 00:19:33,840
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

323
00:19:34,750 --> 00:19:39,280
This is the Chief of Planning.
Send me file number 97 right now.

324
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:41,020
Yes, one moment.

325
00:19:42,920 --> 00:19:44,150
I've sent it, sir.

326
00:19:44,890 --> 00:19:45,890
No problem.

327
00:19:48,490 --> 00:19:49,490
What was that about?

328
00:19:49,930 --> 00:19:53,000
The Chief of Planning asked
for file number 97.

329
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:55,400
What? And you sent it?

330
00:19:56,170 --> 00:19:58,640
- Yes.
- How could you just send it?

331
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:02,010
Darn.

332
00:20:04,070 --> 00:20:05,510
(2026 Cheongma Open Competition:
Rediscovering the Essential)

333
00:20:05,610 --> 00:20:07,480
(Reinterpreting armor's structure
for a modern silhouette)

334
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:11,750
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

335
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,630
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

336
00:20:30,870 --> 00:20:32,800
Isn't that your phone, Ms. Kang?

337
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:36,310
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

338
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:41,580
Hello?

339
00:20:41,850 --> 00:20:43,380
Come to my office right now.

340
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:45,320
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

341
00:20:52,820 --> 00:20:54,020
What is it?

342
00:20:56,260 --> 00:20:58,160
Participant number 97.

343
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:00,800
You said you disqualified them
for violating the guidelines.

344
00:21:01,100 --> 00:21:03,330
What exactly was the violation?

345
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:05,670
If you looked at it, you'd know.

346
00:21:05,740 --> 00:21:07,340
They didn't use the designated font.

347
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:10,470
But fonts are optional,
not mandatory.

348
00:21:10,670 --> 00:21:13,540
A lot of other entries didn't use
the designated font either.

349
00:21:14,380 --> 00:21:16,380
The others looked cohesive,

350
00:21:16,580 --> 00:21:18,650
but the font on number 97
is too distracting.

351
00:21:19,380 --> 00:21:21,080
That's purely subjective,

352
00:21:21,820 --> 00:21:23,950
and I felt
it matched the work nicely.

353
00:21:24,390 --> 00:21:26,160
- Seok Jin.
- So...

354
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:28,460
put it back in the pool for judging.

355
00:21:29,090 --> 00:21:31,090
They put a lot of effort into this.

356
00:21:31,090 --> 00:21:33,200
Isn't it wrong to cut them
over something so minor?

357
00:21:34,630 --> 00:21:36,070
Do you know something, Seok Jin?

358
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:39,600
Know something? What would I know?

359
00:21:42,870 --> 00:21:43,870
Never mind.

360
00:21:45,110 --> 00:21:46,740
We're done here. You can go now.

361
00:22:00,220 --> 00:22:03,260
So, will it be included
in the judging?

362
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:06,130
I don't have a choice.

363
00:22:07,060 --> 00:22:08,800
How's her work?

364
00:22:09,370 --> 00:22:11,570
Is it strong enough
to make it to the finals?

365
00:22:12,370 --> 00:22:14,000
It was actually really well done.

366
00:22:15,440 --> 00:22:18,110
What do I do now?
Isn't there something we can do?

367
00:22:18,180 --> 00:22:20,210
I have to make sure
she gets eliminated.

368
00:22:22,310 --> 00:22:23,680
I'll have to think about it.

369
00:22:27,980 --> 00:22:30,350
(Cheongma)

370
00:22:30,420 --> 00:22:32,490
Thank you for all your hard work
on the judging.

371
00:22:32,990 --> 00:22:34,930
It was my pleasure.

372
00:22:35,360 --> 00:22:37,330
Many of them
exceeded my expectations,

373
00:22:37,430 --> 00:22:39,030
so I really enjoyed
looking through them.

374
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:42,370
Cheongma's future is very bright.

375
00:22:43,730 --> 00:22:45,470
Thank you for saying so.

376
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:49,710
So, are the second-round results
out yet?

377
00:22:50,310 --> 00:22:51,840
As a matter of fact,

378
00:22:51,910 --> 00:22:54,610
there was one contestant
who really caught my eye,

379
00:22:54,710 --> 00:22:56,110
so I'm curious too.

380
00:22:56,380 --> 00:22:58,010
We're finalizing the scores now,

381
00:22:58,080 --> 00:22:59,650
and the announcement
will follow shortly.

382
00:23:01,250 --> 00:23:02,290
Hold on.

383
00:23:03,420 --> 00:23:05,920
Which entry got your attention?

384
00:23:06,790 --> 00:23:08,230
What was the number again?

385
00:23:08,490 --> 00:23:09,660
Number 97.

386
00:23:10,060 --> 00:23:11,660
They were creative...

387
00:23:11,730 --> 00:23:14,730
and showed a precise understanding
of Cheongma's vision.

388
00:23:15,030 --> 00:23:16,130
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

389
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:17,370
Oh, really?

390
00:23:18,900 --> 00:23:21,440
Anyway, I'll organize
a get-together soon.

391
00:23:22,310 --> 00:23:23,340
Sure.

392
00:23:23,510 --> 00:23:24,840
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

393
00:23:40,360 --> 00:23:42,630
(Cheongma Designer Competition:
2nd Round Qualifiers)

394
00:23:44,330 --> 00:23:46,830
Please, 97...

395
00:23:47,030 --> 00:23:51,430
(Entry number, Name,
Last 4 digits of phone number)

396
00:24:05,320 --> 00:24:06,380
Hello?

397
00:24:06,380 --> 00:24:07,520
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

398
00:24:07,580 --> 00:24:09,050
Looks like
they posted the finalists.

399
00:24:09,120 --> 00:24:11,320
How did it go?
Eun Seol, did you make it?

400
00:24:12,620 --> 00:24:14,590
No, I didn't.

401
00:24:15,290 --> 00:24:16,290
Really?

402
00:24:17,030 --> 00:24:18,700
What's your entry number?

403
00:24:19,700 --> 00:24:20,900
Number 97.

404
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:22,700
Number 97...

405
00:24:24,130 --> 00:24:26,370
Your name really isn't up here.

406
00:24:27,300 --> 00:24:29,870
I'm sorry to disappoint you
after all your help.

407
00:24:30,810 --> 00:24:32,940
You have nothing
to apologize to me for.

408
00:24:33,010 --> 00:24:34,140
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

409
00:24:34,140 --> 00:24:35,250
So, what now?

410
00:24:37,180 --> 00:24:38,880
I'll have to figure out
my next move.

411
00:24:45,320 --> 00:24:47,320
(Cheongma Designer Competition:
2nd Round Qualifiers)

412
00:24:48,260 --> 00:24:51,730
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

413
00:24:51,900 --> 00:24:54,430
(Number 16, 22, 27, 41,
55, 68, 73, 95)

414
00:25:01,100 --> 00:25:06,440
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

415
00:25:06,510 --> 00:25:13,480
(Number 97: 92, 93, 91, 94, 0, Fail)

416
00:25:21,090 --> 00:25:22,460
Zero points?

417
00:25:28,600 --> 00:25:32,300
I can't believe I stressed over this
when there was such an easy fix.

418
00:25:32,370 --> 00:25:34,740
Unbelievable. But a zero? Seriously?

419
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:37,770
I told you to just give her
a failing score,

420
00:25:37,840 --> 00:25:39,240
so why did you make it so obvious?

421
00:25:39,840 --> 00:25:41,080
What does it matter?

422
00:25:41,410 --> 00:25:42,950
She failed, and that's fine by me.

423
00:25:44,180 --> 00:25:45,920
Didn't Chief Cha say anything?

424
00:25:46,550 --> 00:25:49,550
What is there for him to say?
I was just exercising my authority.

425
00:25:50,520 --> 00:25:53,760
Anyway,
you saved the day for me again.

426
00:25:54,320 --> 00:25:55,390
Thanks.

427
00:26:04,770 --> 00:26:05,840
- Hey.
- Hello.

428
00:26:05,840 --> 00:26:07,000
- Hello.
- Hello.

429
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:08,040
Right.

430
00:26:09,670 --> 00:26:12,340
But isn't it too bad
about number 97?

431
00:26:12,340 --> 00:26:13,580
Tell me about it.

432
00:26:14,110 --> 00:26:16,450
I wonder why our team leader
gave that entry a zero.

433
00:26:16,580 --> 00:26:18,420
I thought number 97
was the best one.

434
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:20,650
Maybe she deliberately failed them.

435
00:26:21,550 --> 00:26:22,890
Think about it.

436
00:26:22,950 --> 00:26:25,060
Every other judge
scored it above 90,

437
00:26:25,160 --> 00:26:27,060
so her zero points make no sense.

438
00:26:27,460 --> 00:26:29,990
She even tried to get
the entry disqualified, remember?

439
00:26:34,300 --> 00:26:35,570
- Is it good?
- Yes.

440
00:26:37,270 --> 00:26:38,270
What did you say?

441
00:26:38,700 --> 00:26:39,700
Kang Hae Ra did that?

442
00:26:40,070 --> 00:26:41,100
Yes.

443
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:43,340
By the way,
do you know Team Leader Kang?

444
00:26:43,640 --> 00:26:45,140
Unbelievable. Yes.

445
00:26:45,740 --> 00:26:47,280
We went to high school together.

446
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:49,480
Then why...

447
00:26:50,750 --> 00:26:52,250
Was there bad blood between you two?

448
00:26:53,250 --> 00:26:54,320
Yes.

449
00:26:54,820 --> 00:26:56,720
The worst kind.

450
00:27:03,330 --> 00:27:04,730
One moment, please.

451
00:27:05,330 --> 00:27:08,430
Excuse me, Ms. Kang.
The front desk is calling.

452
00:27:08,430 --> 00:27:11,330
Ms. Ko Eun Seol is here to see you.
What should I say?

453
00:27:11,470 --> 00:27:12,640
Who's here?

454
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:14,370
Ms. Ko Eun Seol.

455
00:27:16,140 --> 00:27:17,340
Tell her to leave.

456
00:27:18,240 --> 00:27:19,310
Sure.

457
00:27:20,310 --> 00:27:22,210
Actually, have her sent up.

458
00:27:22,750 --> 00:27:24,250
Right, got it.

459
00:27:25,320 --> 00:27:26,480
Send her up, please.

460
00:27:27,950 --> 00:27:30,090
Why don't you two go get some lunch?

461
00:27:30,820 --> 00:27:31,960
- Sure.
- Okay.

462
00:27:39,830 --> 00:27:41,060
What should we get today?

463
00:27:41,430 --> 00:27:43,570
Stone pot rice or Chinese food?

464
00:27:43,570 --> 00:27:44,700
Chinese food?

465
00:27:45,570 --> 00:27:46,570
Sounds good.

466
00:27:58,750 --> 00:28:00,180
What brings you here?

467
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:03,090
I'm here for my portfolio.

468
00:28:03,790 --> 00:28:06,660
Oh, dear. Don't you know
submissions aren't returned?

469
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:09,090
I'd still like it back.

470
00:28:09,690 --> 00:28:11,090
It's just trash to you anyway.

471
00:28:11,660 --> 00:28:14,100
True. Wait a second.

472
00:28:26,380 --> 00:28:29,110
Shouldn't you say thank you
before taking it?

473
00:28:30,910 --> 00:28:33,350
I know it was you
who ruined my score.

474
00:28:34,020 --> 00:28:35,020
Says who?

475
00:28:35,650 --> 00:28:36,650
Am I wrong?

476
00:28:36,720 --> 00:28:39,090
That's right.
I made sure you failed.

477
00:28:40,020 --> 00:28:41,290
I told you.

478
00:28:41,690 --> 00:28:42,960
As long as I'm around,

479
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:45,300
you'll never get a job here.

480
00:28:48,570 --> 00:28:49,800
We'll see about that.

481
00:28:50,270 --> 00:28:51,270
What?

482
00:28:51,500 --> 00:28:55,310
You think the likes of you
can stop me?

483
00:28:56,170 --> 00:28:58,240
What? The likes of me?

484
00:28:58,810 --> 00:28:59,980
You little...

485
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:03,680
Look at you. Some habits die hard.

486
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:04,710
Let go of me!

487
00:29:05,280 --> 00:29:06,280
Hey.

488
00:29:06,620 --> 00:29:07,880
Listen up.

489
00:29:08,150 --> 00:29:10,920
If I were going to quit now,
I wouldn't have even started.

490
00:29:13,160 --> 00:29:14,820
So what else can you do?

491
00:29:15,630 --> 00:29:16,830
You'll just have to wait and see.

492
00:29:22,730 --> 00:29:24,500
So just you wait.

493
00:29:25,300 --> 00:29:26,970
I'll show you exactly what I can do.

494
00:30:10,680 --> 00:30:14,550
(A Trap Called Desire)

495
00:30:14,620 --> 00:30:17,290
Can you do anything right?

496
00:30:18,090 --> 00:30:21,560
Unbelievable.
She's even crazier than I thought.

497
00:30:21,620 --> 00:30:23,660
Mom, are you seriously praising her
in front of me?

498
00:30:23,690 --> 00:30:24,960
Do you really have to go this far?

499
00:30:25,160 --> 00:30:26,730
This won't change anything.

500
00:30:26,800 --> 00:30:28,230
You'll only end up
looking more pathetic.

501
00:30:28,230 --> 00:30:29,830
Why are you taking it this far?

502
00:30:30,430 --> 00:30:32,140
There's someone
I can't stop thinking about.

503
00:30:32,940 --> 00:30:35,410
Thanks again
for letting us rent the annex.

504
00:30:35,440 --> 00:30:37,810
Don't tell me
they actually ditched me.

505
00:30:38,270 --> 00:30:41,840
If you start giving in,
they'll just keep pushing it.

506
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:43,250
You have to nip it in the bud.

507
00:30:43,480 --> 00:30:45,750
- What are you going to do now?
- I've got to give it a shot.

508
00:30:45,750 --> 00:30:46,850
Speaking of which...

509
00:30:47,120 --> 00:30:48,420
It was originally mine.

510
00:30:48,590 --> 00:30:49,920
I'm just taking it back.

511
00:30:51,120 --> 00:30:53,120
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
